  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 140 PM MDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nMain impact through tomorrow will be smoke impact with Air\nQuality Alerts in effect for several counties. Strong west to\nsouthwest flow has brought in the smoke and expect it to remain\nMonday as flow aloft shifts more northwesterly with several\nwestern wildfires ongoing. Many Red Flag warnings still in\neffect as well due to wind and humidity through this evening. \nWill see significant cooling on Monday as an upper level trof \nworks east through Idaho. Highs only in the lower 80s low \nelevations and 70s mountains. The below normal temperatures will\ncontinue through Tuesday then another warming trend begins \nWednesday with low elevation high temperatures well into the 90s\nagain by thursday with very hot conditions expected through \nnext weekend once again. Will likely see upper 90s by next \nweekend in the lower elevations. Forecast grids have no \nprecipitation anywhere through next Sunday.",
